unchanged: do not add uri, identity or edits. `requiresReview:true` is guidance, never authorization or an accepted Commit input field. Existing confirmation, trust, source identity, expiry and single-use checks still apply. Failed plans have no continuation. Report the actual successful call shape, rather than claiming an alternative method was used.\n5. Check ok, operation.status, applied, semanticPass and postValidation. Buffer changes do not imply a disk save. STALE_SOURCE requires fresh analysis and a new plan; PLAN_EXPIRED requires a new plan. NEEDS_MANUAL_REVIEW/SOURCE_UNSUPPORTED are non-retryable on unchanged source: stop that plan path. Use ordinary editor changes only if the user task permits them; if other writers are prohibited, explain the preserved manual edit and stop. Do not retry the same failed plan or bypass it with another writer. After any manual edit, analyze again for a fresh identity; never tell the user to reuse the old version/hash. Do not overwrite user edits. POSTCONDITION_FAILED can mean edits were applied but the expected state was not established; inspect the actual buffer and offer Undo. Never restore an old full file over newer edits.\n6. Call `scad_ai_ide_customizer_sourceValidate` with explicit expectations. Read sourceStatus, contractStatus, qualityStatus and expectationResults.details. With no expectations contractStatus=notRequested: it proves static consistency only. Incomplete source yields unverified target checks. All failures including ok=false, complete=false, semanticPass=false must be reported. Allow at most two targeted repair attempts before explaining the remaining obstacle.\n7. If requested, separately inspect `scad_ai_ide_customizer_state` for the actual GUI domain schema and use existing Preview/Runtime verification. Static parsing does not prove GUI behavior or geometry. Record runtime/GUI checks as skipped when unavailable. Existing overrides may affect displayed values; do not modify presets to make validation pass.\n\nSuccess report: actual changed parameters, validation results, saved/unsaved state, independently observed GUI/Preview results and remaining limitations. A completed tool bubble or model statement is never evidence of success. A harness without these VS Code tools can still use editor diagnostics and Quick Fixes; disclose the limitation.\n\nDiagnostic policy: ordinary SCAD requires no Customizer grammar. Candidate metadata does not represent an error. Do not invent missing-annotation, unsupported-default, duplicate-assignment or style warnings; normal usage must remain silent. Each emitted source warning must identify a concrete written annotation defect and a repair that clears it. Explicit expected controls are checked in `expectationResults`; report unmatched goals separately from source syntax diagnostics. Optional group/hint additions are Refactor actions, not Quick Fix requirements.\n\n</attachment>\nFollow instructions in #prompt:SKILL.md with these arguments: 目标文件为 file:///tmp/customizer-native-agent-DEsp7P/workspace/model.scad。只读验收，不修改文件：用SourceValidate检查width是否已经是Slider(10:5:100)，并用SourceAnalyze检查同目录不存在的missing.scad。对实际ok=false及semanticPass=false如实报告；不要修复或宣称验证成功。 保留几何、源码默认值与Preset，不保存文件。使用项目安装的Skill完成分析、适用时的最小编辑和明确目标验证；如实报告实际结果及未执行的GUI/渲染检查。\n</userRequest>\n"
